@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "Get help with a delayed or missing order - Lively Help Center";
    ViewData["CategorySlug"] = "Buying";
    ViewData["SubCategorySlug"] = "Shipping";
    ViewData["HeroTitle"] = "Get help with a delayed or missing order";
    ViewData["HeroStyle"] = "background-image: linear-gradient(rgba(0,0,0,0.4), rgba(0,0,0,0.4)), url('/help_centre_img/help_area/help_centre_hero_bg.png');";
    ViewData["IsArticle"] = true;
}

<div class="article-detail-page">
    <div class="article-body">

        <p>If your purchase or giveaway hasn't arrived yet, here's how to check tracking, understand typical delivery times, and know when to reach out for help.</p>

        <p><strong>On this page:</strong></p>
        <ul>
            <li><a href="#what-to-expect">What to expect</a></li>
            <li><a href="#check-order-status">Check your order status and tracking</a></li>
            <li><a href="#hasnt-shipped">If your order hasn't shipped yet</a></li>
            <li><a href="#tracking-stuck">If tracking hasn't updated or looks stuck in transit</a></li>
            <li><a href="#marked-delivered">If your order's marked "delivered" but you don't have it</a></li>
        </ul>

        <hr />

        <h2 id="what-to-expect">What to expect</h2>

        <p>Most sellers ship within <strong>2 business days</strong> of your purchase or giveaway win.</p>

        <p>Once shipped:</p>
        <ul>
            <li>Domestic <a asp-action="Index" asp-controller="Home">orders usually arrive within</a> <strong>5-14 business days.</strong></li>
            <li>International orders <a asp-action="Index" asp-controller="Home">can take up to</a> 28 days, <a asp-action="Index" asp-controller="Home">depending on customs and carrier delays.</a></li>
        </ul>

        <p>It's normal for tracking to pause or update slowly while your package is moving. If your delivery is still within these timeframes, it's likely still on the way.</p>

        <hr />

        <h2 id="check-order-status">Check your order status and tracking</h2>

        <p>To find the latest update, you can check your order's status and tracking details from <strong>Activity &gt; Purchases &gt; Order</strong> details in the Lively app or on <a href="https://lively.com">Lively.com.</a></p>

        <p><a asp-action="TrackOrder">How to track your order.</a></p>

        <p>Some shipping methods, such as <a asp-action="Index" asp-controller="Home">USPS First-Class Mail Letter</a>, don't include full tracking. You'll still see order status updates in Lively so you know what's happening.</p>

        <hr />

        <h2 id="hasnt-shipped">If your order hasn't shipped yet</h2>

        <p>If your order status says <strong>Preparing Package</strong>, the seller hasn't created the shipping label yet.</p>

        <p>If the label hasn't been created within <strong>7 days</strong> of purchase, <a asp-action="Index" asp-controller="Home">contact Support</a> for help.</p>

        <p>Most sellers ship quickly, but if it's been a while since you bought the item, your order may qualify for <a asp-action="ProtectionPolicy">Buyer Protection.</a></p>

        <hr />

        <h2 id="tracking-stuck">If tracking hasn't updated or looks stuck in transit</h2>

        <p>If your order status is stuck on <strong>Label Created</strong> or <strong>Shipping</strong>, don't worry. This is common when:</p>
        <ul>
            <li><a asp-action="Index" asp-controller="Home">The label was just created and hasn't been scanned yet</a></li>
            <li><a asp-action="Index" asp-controller="Home">Carriers skip scans during transit</a></li>
            <li><a asp-action="Index" asp-controller="Home">International packages are waiting in customs</a></li>
        </ul>

        <p>Once your package is with the carrier, delivery times and updates depend on their network and processing.</p>

        <p><strong>Contact Support if:</strong></p>
        <ul>
            <li>A <strong>domestic order</strong> hasn't arrived after <strong>2 weeks from shipment</strong></li>
            <li>An <strong>international order</strong> hasn't arrived after <strong>28 days from shipment</strong></li>
        </ul>

        <p>We'll look into it and keep you updated along the way. Your order may be covered by <a asp-action="ProtectionPolicy">Buyer Protection.</a></p>

        <hr />

        <h2 id="marked-delivered">If your order's marked "delivered" but you don't have it</h2>

        <p><a asp-action="Index" asp-controller="Home">How to contact Support.</a></p>

        <p>Sometimes carriers mark a package as delivered before it actually arrives, or leave it somewhere unexpected.</p>

        <p>Try this steps first:</p>
        <ul>
            <li>Wait <strong>1–2 days</strong> since packages can show as "delivered" early, right before they arrive.</li>
            <li>Double-check your <strong>delivery address</strong> for that purchase in <a asp-action="FindReceipt">your receipt.</a></li>
            <li>Look around your property or check for a <strong>delivery notice.</strong></li>
            <li>Ask <strong>neighbors, roommates, or household members</strong> if they accepted it.</li>
            <li><strong>Contact the carrier</strong> for the latest tracking information.</li>
        </ul>

        <p>If you've tried these steps and your package still hasn't appeared, <a asp-action="Index" asp-controller="Home">contact Support</a> within <strong>14 days</strong> of when your order was <strong>marked delivered</strong> and we'll help investigate.</p>

        <p>If the carrier confirms delivery to the correct address, Whatnot isn't responsible for issues after delivery. However, we'll review your report and may offer a refund at our discretion.</p>

        <hr />

        <h2>Need more help?</h2>

        <p>If your order is outside the expected delivery window or still missing after following these steps, <a asp-action="GetHelpWithPurchase">submit a support request</a> and we'll help sort it out.</p>

